6?</strong></span><br><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Answer.&nbsp;</strong>You can check it on the official UPSC website.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Q. What should I search on the website to find the UPSC NDA/ NA-II Admit Card 2026?</strong></span><br><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Answer.</strong>&nbsp;Look for&nbsp;<strong>“Admit Card – UPSC NDA/ NA-II Recruitment 2026”</strong>&nbsp;in the notifications list</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Q. What details are required to download the admit card?</strong></span><br><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Answer.&nbsp;</strong>Candidates need their&nbsp;<strong>Registration Number / Roll Number</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Password / Captcha</strong>&nbsp;to download the admit card.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Q. What is UPSC Official Website? <br></strong><strong>Answer. </strong>The Official Website of UPSC is https://upsc.gov.in</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n",
